    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316">

                <pb facs="0520" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg424"/>

                <head>No. 316.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Nelson.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-05-22"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 22,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 249.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit herewith a copy of the
                    correspondence between this Department and Mr. Thomas F. Wilson, consul of the
                    United States at <pb facs="0521" n="425" xml:id="pg425"/> Matamoras,’in relation
                    to the eighth article of the proclamation of General Palacio, under date of the
                    8th ultimo, which provides for the exercise of surveillance upon vessels
                    navigating the Bravo Bio Grande.</p>
                <p>You will be pleased to read to the minister for foreign affairs of Mexico the
                    instruction addressed on the 17th instant (No. 54) by this Department to Mr.
                    Wilson.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>







